1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,627
Throw a paper ball into a bin.

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:03,860
Kick a football.

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:06,027
Spray water from a garden hose.

4
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:09,143
Three different things,
one same kind of curve.

5
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:11,850
Aarav noticed it at his study table.

6
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:14,115
He flicked a paper ball at the bin.

7
00:00:14,465 --> 00:00:17,435
It rose, turned, and
dropped in one smooth curve.

8
00:00:17,435 --> 00:00:19,534
Is that curve a piece of a circle?

9
00:00:20,034 --> 00:00:23,700
By the end, you will know its
exact shape, and prove it yourself.

10
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:26,141
So what is a trajectory?

11
00:00:26,491 --> 00:00:29,462
It is the path a projectile
traces in the air.

12
00:00:29,462 --> 00:00:32,735
Every point on it is a
pair of numbers, x and y.

13
00:00:33,135 --> 00:00:35,256
We already have two equations.

14
00:00:35,256 --> 00:00:37,129
One gives x at any time.

15
00:00:37,129 --> 00:00:38,195
One gives y.

16
00:00:38,595 --> 00:00:41,070
But a path does not care about time.

17
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:45,161
To get its shape, we remove
time, and write y using only x.

18
00:00:45,811 --> 00:00:48,308
Let's launch a ball in
our motion notebook.

19
00:00:48,658 --> 00:00:52,458
It leaves at twenty metres per
second, at forty five degrees.

20
00:00:52,858 --> 00:00:55,499
Across, the blue part never changes.

21
00:00:55,499 --> 00:00:58,645
So x grows in equal steps, in equal times.

22
00:00:59,045 --> 00:01:03,429
Up and down, the violet part shrinks,
because gravity pulls down all the

23
00:01:03,429 --> 00:01:04,329
time.

24
00:01:04,359 --> 00:01:06,067
Slow motion at the top.

25
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:08,137
The violet part is zero here.

26
00:01:08,137 --> 00:01:10,106
Only the blue part is left.

27
00:01:10,606 --> 00:01:14,744
On the graph, the dot draws y
against x, as the ball flies.

28
00:01:15,394 --> 00:01:18,477
Now let's find its equation,
one step at a time.

29
00:01:18,827 --> 00:01:19,727
Step one.

30
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:22,169
Across, there is no acceleration.

31
00:01:22,169 --> 00:01:25,266
So x equals v naught cos theta, times t.

32
00:01:26,016 --> 00:01:26,953
Step two.

33
00:01:26,953 --> 00:01:28,301
Turn it around.

34
00:01:28,301 --> 00:01:32,073
Time t equals x, divided
by v naught cos theta.

35
00:01:32,823 --> 00:01:33,841
Step three.

36
00:01:33,841 --> 00:01:39,443
Up and down, y equals v naught sin
theta times t, minus half g t squared.

37
00:01:40,193 --> 00:01:41,093
Step four.

38
00:01:41,046 --> 00:01:43,831
Put this t from step two into step three.

39
00:01:44,581 --> 00:01:47,006
The first part becomes x tan theta.

40
00:01:47,006 --> 00:01:51,706
The second part becomes g x squared,
over two v naught squared cos squared

41
00:01:51,706 --> 00:01:52,606
theta.

42
00:01:53,118 --> 00:01:54,164
Remember this.

43
00:01:54,164 --> 00:01:57,891
Remove time, and the path of
a projectile is a parabola.

44
00:01:58,591 --> 00:01:59,653
Why a parabola?

45
00:01:59,653 --> 00:02:01,788
Look at the shape of the equation.

46
00:02:02,138 --> 00:02:05,733
For one throw, theta, v
naught and g are fixed.

47
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:08,525
So y equals a x, minus b x squared.

48
00:02:08,925 --> 00:02:12,949
The a x part alone is a straight
line, along the launch direction.

49
00:02:13,349 --> 00:02:17,528
The minus b x squared part
pulls it down, more as x grows.

50
00:02:17,528 --> 00:02:18,804
That is gravity.

51
00:02:18,804 --> 00:02:21,428
A line bent like this is a parabola.

52
00:02:22,078 --> 00:02:23,184
Side by side.

53
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:25,293
With no gravity, b is zero.

54
00:02:25,293 --> 00:02:28,191
The ball flies in a straight line forever.

55
00:02:28,591 --> 00:02:30,923
With gravity, the line bends down.

56
00:02:30,923 --> 00:02:35,209
The far end drops the most, because
the drop grows with x squared.

57
00:02:35,809 --> 00:02:36,853
Now you try.

58
00:02:36,853 --> 00:02:39,823
A ball rolls off a table, straight across.

59
00:02:39,823 --> 00:02:41,545
Is its path a parabola?

60
00:02:41,545 --> 00:02:42,843
Pause and decide.

61
00:02:46,043 --> 00:02:46,943
Yes!

62
00:02:46,609 --> 00:02:49,527
Theta is zero, so tan theta is zero.

63
00:02:49,527 --> 00:02:53,644
y equals minus g x squared,
over two v naught squared.

64
00:02:53,644 --> 00:02:55,586
That is half a parabola.

65
00:02:56,236 --> 00:02:57,985
What changes the curve?

66
00:02:57,985 --> 00:02:58,976
Look at b.

67
00:02:59,326 --> 00:03:02,053
v naught squared sits at the bottom of b.

68
00:03:02,053 --> 00:03:05,558
Throw twice as fast, and b
becomes four times smaller.

69
00:03:05,958 --> 00:03:08,484
So a faster throw bends more slowly.

70
00:03:08,484 --> 00:03:10,795
Its parabola is wider and taller.

71
00:03:11,395 --> 00:03:12,295
Your turn.

72
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:15,864
Both leave at forty five
degrees, one twice as fast.

73
00:03:15,864 --> 00:03:18,350
Ten metres across, which is higher?

74
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:19,594
Pause and think.

75
00:03:22,794 --> 00:03:23,924
The faster one!

76
00:03:23,924 --> 00:03:25,993
Both start along the same line.

77
00:03:25,993 --> 00:03:29,948
But the faster ball has a smaller
b, so it has dropped less.

78
00:03:30,598 --> 00:03:32,334
Now, one worked example.

79
00:03:32,684 --> 00:03:37,154
A ball is thrown at twenty metres
per second, at forty five degrees.

80
00:03:37,154 --> 00:03:39,591
How high is it, ten metres across?

81
00:03:40,091 --> 00:03:45,144
At forty five degrees, tan theta is
one, and cos squared theta is one half.

82
00:03:45,894 --> 00:03:50,878
So b equals nine point eight, over
two times four hundred times one half.

83
00:03:50,878 --> 00:03:53,587
That is zero point zero two four five.

84
00:03:54,337 --> 00:03:55,834
Put x equals ten.

85
00:03:55,834 --> 00:04:00,897
y equals ten, minus zero point zero
two four five times one hundred.

86
00:04:01,647 --> 00:04:04,464
y equals ten minus two point four five.

87
00:04:04,464 --> 00:04:07,712
The ball is seven point
five five metres high.

88
00:04:08,362 --> 00:04:09,827
Now, the exam trap.

89
00:04:10,177 --> 00:04:14,649
Many students write cos theta at the
bottom, instead of cos squared theta.

90
00:04:14,999 --> 00:04:17,729
But t was squared, in half g t squared.

91
00:04:17,729 --> 00:04:22,132
So the whole t gets squared, and
cos theta becomes cos squared theta.

92
00:04:22,782 --> 00:04:24,080
Where is this asked?

93
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:28,210
You get a trajectory equation, and
find the angle or the speed from it.

94
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,070
Exam level now.

95
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:35,402
A projectile moves along y equals root
three x, minus x squared over twenty.

96
00:04:35,402 --> 00:04:36,342
g is ten.

97
00:04:36,342 --> 00:04:38,543
Find the angle and the speed.

98
00:04:38,543 --> 00:04:39,858
Pause and solve.

99
00:04:45,258 --> 00:04:46,523
The answer is A.

100
00:04:46,523 --> 00:04:49,438
Sixty degrees, and
twenty metres per second.

101
00:04:49,938 --> 00:04:52,559
Match it with y equals x tan theta.

102
00:04:52,559 --> 00:04:56,259
Tan theta is root three,
so theta is sixty degrees.

103
00:04:56,759 --> 00:05:01,898
Next, g over two v naught squared cos
squared theta equals one over twenty.

104
00:05:01,898 --> 00:05:06,611
Cos squared sixty is one quarter,
so v naught squared is four hundred,

105
00:05:06,611 --> 00:05:08,380
and v naught is twenty.

106
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,436
Here is your recap.

107
00:05:10,436 --> 00:05:11,933
Screenshot this card.

108
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:18,132
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

109
00:05:18,532 --> 00:05:19,432
One.

110
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,282
Why do we remove time to
find the shape of the path?

111
00:05:23,182 --> 00:05:24,082
Two.

112
00:05:23,701 --> 00:05:27,309
In the trajectory equation,
why is cos theta squared?

113
00:05:28,209 --> 00:05:29,109
Three.

114
00:05:28,725 --> 00:05:31,475
What would the path be
if there were no gravity?

115
00:05:32,575 --> 00:05:35,769
Next time: same speed,
thirty degrees or sixty.

116
00:05:35,769 --> 00:05:37,823
Which stays in the air longer?

117
00:05:37,823 --> 00:05:39,732
Find out in time of flight.
